    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895">

                <pb facs="0942" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/192:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-16T10:00:00-05:45">July 16, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>139. Supplementing my 137, July 13, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d895-f1"/>
                    there have been persistent rumors for some days of a considerable bandit
                    movement towards the east coast. The Guardia is endeavoring to develop the
                    situation and the air forces are cooperating.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
